  "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit. Edit image 1, the existing NW-facing three-quarter rear running boy, in exactly its original square transparent canvas. Output one native square RGBA PNG at least 1024x1024, with transparent clear margins on all four edges. Image 2 (NW14) and image 3 (NW16) are neighboring-frame ankle-axis references only; image 4 is the approved painted-material/style reference, not a composition. LOCAL CHANGE ONLY: correct the anatomical LEFT airborne boot of the near bent leg at lower screen-left in image 1. Preserve its knee position, trouser shape, ankle opening and heel center; keep its current raised swing phase. Redraw the ankle-to-foot connection and foot orientation to stay in the same NW fore-aft motion plane as this leg and the adjacent reference frames. The existing foot has an isolated nearly horizontal sideways kick silhouette between the naturally diagonal soles in images 2 and 3. Remove that lateral twist: use a smooth diagonal heel-to-forefoot longitudinal axis consistent with a knee-bent NW stride, with the forefoot naturally extending down-left from the heel in this perspective, not sharply sideways. Preserve natural plantar flexion and physically plausible visible sole, not a flat sticker or an attempt to hide all sole. This is only foot orientation, not moving the knee or entire leg. The anatomical RIGHT ground-supporting leg and boot at lower screen-right are locked. Do not change support position, leg spacing, body position or phase. Everything else from image 1 is locked: exact head, hair, body, hips, robe, both arms and hands, right-hand brush and its one attached teal tassel, left-hand blank scroll, exactly two cyan ink spirits, camera, lighting, silhouette scale and canvas placement. Preserve the crisp rich hand-painted black/gold/teal costume. No new background, floor, shadow, diagram, label, text, or additional objects.",
