  "prompt": "Precise local animation edit. Image1 editable calligrapher boy, image2 approved archer SAME-DIRECTION anatomy reference only, image3 approved style. Latest motion requirement OVERRIDES reference phase timing: SAME FOOT stays actually planted through 8 consecutive frames, four progressively rearward support locations with 2 distinct poses each, then other foot supports. Never copy a frame or move entire picture to fake ground. Keep native1254 transparent square, stable head/body volume and camera/framing, identity/costume. RIGHT brush with connected single teal tassel, LEFT scroll plus TWO cyan ink spirits. Pants cover legs. Knee, ankle and boot longitudinal axis must point along travel direction, without toe-out or lateral ankle roll. Natural knee flexion; no mechanically locked straight knee. Preserve all upper body/props; local trouser-leg/shoe motion only, no drawn ground/shadow.\nImage4 is the next near-left-contact boy frame only for lookahead, not editable target. Latest user same support remains all half-cycle.\nLOCAL TASK: Edit image1 NW late RIGHT stance. Actual near anatomical LEFT thigh is folded at screen-left foreground and its sole faces back; far RIGHT long leg is grounded at screen-right lower. Preserve these hip identities. FIRST of FOURTH support-position pair. Keep far-right broad forefoot planted at same rear location, only lift heel10-12degrees. Near-left swing boot comes forward/up-left, ankle dorsiflexed, shoe long-axis NW, sole edge about1070y and clearly airborne; do not show a sideways kicked sole. This is prior to next contact. Stable head/body/robe and hands; right brush left scroll with2spirits. Small natural left-scroll arm advances toward front/up-left20px, far-right brush elbow recedes slightly20px, no prop swapping. Do not recompose. Native transparent square.",
